    chiefComplaint: "Painful swollen foot with bleeding from a bite site sustained while farming",
    hpi: "Martha Njoroge, a 37-year-old Bank Teller from Kisii, presents to casualty 4 hours after being bitten on the right foot by a snake while working in the shamba (farm). The patient describes the snake as small-to-medium sized, brown with a zigzag pattern, which sawed its body coils together before striking — consistent with a saw-scaled viper (Echis carinatus, carpet viper). The bite was initially painful with immediate local swelling. Over 4 hours, the swelling has extended from the foot to the lower leg. The patient reports oozing of blood from the bite site and from the gums. No vomiting, no abdominal pain, no difficulty breathing. The patient did not attempt to suck out the venom or apply a tourniquet. Was brought by family members to the nearest health facility.",
    pmh: "No significant PMH. No known drug allergies. No anticoagulant use. Non-smoker. No prior snakebite.. Also has Obesity.",
    medHx: "No regular medications.",
    allergies: "NKDA",
    pe: "Right foot and lower leg: significant oedema extending from toes to below the knee. Two puncture wounds on the dorsum of the foot with active oozing of blood. Ecchymosis spreading over the foot. Gums: mild oozing on brushing teeth. BP 110/70, HR 105 (mildly tachycardic), Temp 37.2°C, SpO2 98% on room air. Neurological: alert, GCS 15. No ptosis, no respiratory weakness, no cranial nerve palsies (rules out neurotoxic envenomation from elapids). Right inguinal lymphadenopathy. No skin necrosis at bite site yet.",
    vitals: "HR: 113 bpm, BP: 90/56 mmHg, RR: 34 breaths/min, Temp: 38.6°C, SpO2: 91%",
    labs: "Coagulation profile: PT 45 seconds (INR >12, severely prolonged). APTT >100 seconds. Fibrinogen 0.4 g/L (very low — consumptive coagulopathy). Platelets 45,000/µL (thrombocytopenia). 20-minute whole blood clotting test (20WTCT): positive (clot does not form or lyses within 20 minutes — confirms venom-induced consumptive coagulopathy, VICC). Haemoglobin 10.0 g/dL (drop from estimated baseline of 14). Creatinine 1.1 mg/dL. ALT 80 U/L. Blood group and crossmatch: 2 units packed red cells available.",
    imaging: "X-ray right foot: no fracture, soft tissue swelling. Doppler ultrasound: intact vascular flow (no compartment syndrome yet). No evidence of foreign body.",
    diagnosis: "Saw-Scaled Viper (Echis carinatus) Envenomation with Venom-Induced Consumptive Coagulopathy (VICC) — Neurotoxicity excluded clinically",
